{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates the variance of each lottery and prefers the one with higher variance. Variance can be calculated from the outcomes and their probabilities. For Lottery A: outcomes are 4000 (25%), 2000 (25%), and 0 (50%). The expected value is (0.25×4000) + (0.25×2000) + (0.5×0) = 1000 + 500 + 0 = 1500. Variance = Σp_i × (x_i - E)^2 = 0.25×(4000-1500)² + 0.25×(2000-1500)² + 0.5×(0-1500)² = 0.25×6,250,000 + 0.25×250,000 + 0.5×2,250,000 = 1,562,500 + 62,500 + 1,125,000 = 2,750,000. For Lottery B: outcomes are 6000 (25%) and 0 (75%). Expected value = 0.25×6000 = 1500. Variance = 0.25×(6000-1500)² + 0.75×(0-1500)² = 0.25×20,250,000 + 0.75×2,250,000 = 5,062,500 + 1,687,500 = 6,750,000. Thus, Lottery B has a higher variance (6,750,000) than Lottery A (2,750,000). The decision reason would prefer Lottery B due to higher variance.",
